x676c: serialize command-mode DSI triggers and use TOPRGU diagnostic reset

The captured source and panel-memory hashes match and the final thumbnail has
a clock/home indicator, but the physical panel stays at the logo. DSI INTSTA
retains BUSY. Follow the vendor trigger's mutex enable, DSI engine reset and
START ordering; avoid retriggering while busy and the duplicate present/vsync
trigger. Register writes use explicit barriers. Physical output still requires
validation after this change.

The diagnostic PSCI reset returned unchanged. Use the MT6789 vendor watchdog
software-reset key after syncing, restricted to the X676C compatible string.
The new reset path still requires hardware validation.

